From 0df90c0a2d2eb96c4043c47e8833c7bdd6068eb7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:37:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: one large scratch artifact under two
 spellings no longer crashes completion

Follow-up t_01a1da75a3adee08 from the exact-head review of PR #2992
(t_01a1da701fe99096).

Symptom: a managed-scratch file over KANBAN_ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES declared
under two spellings that normalize to one path (`<ws>/x.bin` plus
`<ws>/./x.bin`, or an artifact plus a `~/...` completion_receipt evidence
ref) made complete_task / request_review raise
`AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'rename'`. The card
stayed running and every retry with the same metadata failed again. Base
(350667116f) copied the file twice and completed.

Why:
1. record_files iterates raw declared strings; declared_files dedupes only
   textually, so both spellings get a record.
2. kanban_artifact_prestage keys its cache by the expanded path, so both
   records `take()` the same entry.
3. The first `_large` renamed the staged copy and set `temp = None`; the
   second called `None.rename`.
4. AttributeError is outside record_files' (OSError,
   ArtifactPreservationError) handler, so it escaped unclassified.
Second defect found by the same test: `_fill` read the file once per
spelling and overwrote the cache entry, orphaning the first `.prestage-*`
copy (never claimed, never unlinked) and doubling the pre-lock read.

Fix:
- `_large` records the claimed `retained_path` on the prestage entry; a
  later record for the same entry reuses it (and its sha256). A managed
  entry with neither a claim nor a staged copy now fails closed with
  ArtifactPreservationError instead of AttributeError.
- `_fill` skips a path already in the cache: one read, one copy.

Proof (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_artifact_custody_bounds.py):
- RED at bb425a47e5: test_large_scratch_file_named_under_two_spellings_
  is_retained_once[artifact|evidence] and test_managed_large_file_without_
  a_pre_lock_copy_fails_closed fail with the reported AttributeError.
- With only the `_large` fix, both spelling cases fail on a leaked
  `.prestage-*` file (kills removal of the `_fill` skip).
- GREEN: 6 artifact/receipt/metadata test files, 60 passed.
- scripts/check: 20 checks ok.
